  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Legal Application**\n\nI\'m focusing on defining the scope for \"BDCM ABOGADOS\" legal application. It will need to incorporate Chilean legal specifics like RUT numbers, relevant courts (Tribunales, Cortes, Juzgados), and handle Labor, Family, Guarantee, and TOP matters. I am working on the initial requirements analysis now.\n\n\n**Expanding the Data Model**\n\nI\'m now expanding the data model, integrating crucial elements. This encompasses features for small law firm management, including client details (RUT, contact info, associated cases), case management (ROL/RIT/RUC, tribunal, matter type, status), and tracking deadlines (fatal/non-fatal, due dates, calculations). I\'m also including functionalities for hearings, meetings (type, court, virtual/in-person details), and fee management (agreed amount, payment installments).\n\n\n**Adding New Features**\n\nI am currently working on crucial additions. This involves fee installment management (due date, payment status, receipts, firm financial balance), synchronization with Google Calendar (leveraging the Workspace integration/Google Calendar API for hearings, deadlines, and meetings, including .ics file generation and browser notifications), and the design of an intuitive interface (premium, responsive across devices, fast search, urgent deadline widgets). Additionally, a draft generator, procedural activity log, and Chilean legal deadline calculator are in progress.\n\n\n"
