  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing the App Concept**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the core functionalities needed for a legal office app. I\'ve broken down the requirements into modules: client management, case tracking, fee calculation, appointment scheduling, deadline reminders, and payment tracking. I\'m prioritizing user experience and efficient data entry for lawyers. I\'m exploring different database structures for optimal performance and data integrity.\n\n\n**Defining App Integration Needs**\n\nI\'m now identifying the essential integration requirements, specifically for Google Calendar synchronization and automated notifications within the legal app. The firm, BDCM ABOGADOS, operates in Chile, so I need to factor in this region. This will involve the use of OAuth for Google Calendar and setting the minimal scopes needed, and will require a call with userConfirmedInUI set to false.\n\n\n**Refining OAuth Flow Design**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the precise OAuth flow. It\'s critical that the application *always* initially calls the tool with `userConfirmedInUI: false`. I must then wait for the accept/decline response before proceeding. If the user accepts, I\342\200\231ll call the tool again with `userConfirmedInUI: true`. Should they decline, I\342\200\231ll stop there. This is vital to uphold user trust. I\'m also confirming the specific text for the initial prompt, including the product name \"Google Calendar,\" the capability description (in Spanish for the firm\'s location), the explicit permission statement and reference to the card.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_38387"
