  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Requirements & Constraints**\n\nI\'ve outlined the initial requirements. My focus is now on the first turn: updating `metadata.json` with the project name and description, and then synchronizing those values with the HTML title and meta description. It\'s crucial that the project name, once set, is never changed, so I need to factor that into the overall strategy.\n\n\n**Adding Open Graph Tags**\n\nI\'m now integrating Open Graph tags (`og:title`, `og:description`) into `index.html`. My focus extends to incorporating law firm details: \"BDCM ABOGADOS\" - Chile. I\'m moving toward a robust system for managing a comprehensive legal practice. Specifically, I\'m defining data structures for \'Clientes\' (Clients), including validations for Chilean RUT numbers, and then \'Causas / Expedientes Judiciales\' (Cases) with fields for ROL, Tribunal, and Materia (Matter). I will consider the quality (Plaintiff/Defendant) as part of that structure, too.\n\n\n**Defining Legal Case Data**\n\nI\'m now diving into the detailed data structures needed for \'Causas / Expedientes Judiciales\' (Cases). I\'m defining key fields: the *Calidad* (quality) of the parties involved (ante / Solicitante / Querellante / Patrocinante vs Demandado / Imputado / Recurrido), the *Estado Procesal* (processing state) with several options, the *Abogado Responsable / Patrocinante* (responsible lawyer), and the *Cuant\303\255a* (amount) in Chilean Pesos (CLP) or UF. I\'m also planning for a *Bit\303\241cora Procesal* (procedural log) for tracking events and relevant documents. Finally, I\'m thinking about integrations with the Poder Judicial (PJUD).\n\n\n**Prioritizing Visual Cues**\n\nI\'m now focusing on visual urgency indicators: red for overdue, flashing orange for today\'s deadlines, yellow for the next three days, and green for on-time. I\'m also structuring data for hearings and meetings. This includes type (e.g., Oral Trial), tribunal/location, modality (including direct connection links for teleconferences), date/time, and preparation details. I\'m integrating with Google Calendar via API for instant synchronization. I\'m additionally designing billing and installment tracking, incorporating honorarium types and payment statuses, with payment methods.\n\n\n**Integrating Financial Tools**\n\nI\'m now integrating financial tools. I\'m focusing on features such as tracking honorarium invoices and payment dates. I\'ll include a financial dashboard that summarizes total billed/agreed fees, collected amounts, outstanding balance, and overdue installments, along with a monthly projection. My main focus is to ensure easy access to all financial details.\n\n\n"
